{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf","id":1429124,"title":"Kingdom of the Bull of the Norf'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-20T01:28:38-08:00","id":1429124,"title":"Kingdom of the Bull of the Norf'","content":"Where in your campaigns have you put the Bull of the Norf' and his war with house Tepet? what is the size of his dominion and how has it grown as the game progressed? How has it affected canon locations and cities?<br /> I'm asking this because as necessary as Yurgen and his funnyboys are to the set-up of exalted, his victory over the realm seem to have no impact on places like pneuma, whitewall, or the kingdom of medo in their description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T02:45:55-08:00","id":1429127,"title":"","content":"I actually am not running an Exalted campaign, but as far as I can tell the Bull of the North is mostly a sideline to the main campaign (so far), far removed from the politics of the Imperial City. His main impact is that he broke the power of House Tepet over the Imperial legions. But this could change if the Bull\u2019s armies press southward past the Threshold into the Realm itself.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Now you\u2019ve got me curious lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T04:43:32-08:00","id":1429132,"title":"","content":"It does seem like old Bully is just there to be the reason why rolling Tepet is such a bad deal. Still pneuma should be living in fear of his frozen horde, but nothing is mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T04:58:34-08:00","id":1429133,"title":"","content":"They didn\u2019t think through the implications of the Bull\u2019s actions.<br /> <br /> Pneuma means lung. Or maybe rubber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T05:28:39-08:00","id":1429136,"title":"","content":"We had this on the Discord a <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/205962784599441408/390888639241912340/780164250097811497\" target=\"_blank\">couple of weeks ago</a>.<br /> <br /> The Bull is way up by the White Sea and on both sides of Mela's Fangs -- East and North of Malice Bay (the mouth of the River of Tears where it opens into the White Sea). The Bull's Icewalker nomads (who, you know, <i>walk</i> everywhere) are over a thousand miles away from Whitewall and Pneuma.<br /> <br /> He is pretty close to Medo though -- if he were to sail down the River of Tears, they could probably make it there in a couple of days. But, they have to cross one of the largest &quot;rivers&quot;* in Creation to get to Medo.<br /> <br /> He's up in the Far North with the Haslanti League.<br /> <br /> (He used to be West and South of Malice Bay (North of Cherak and East of Whitewall), which put him a lot closer to Whitewall. And, of course, when the 1E fluff was written, the map was smaller. So there is some old fluff about him interacting with these places and Whitewall worrying/hoping that he might invade.)<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> *The River of Tears is an oddly shaped artificial sea (into which the Yanaze, Avarice, and Silver rivers flow). It's not a &quot;river&quot; in any meaningful sense of the word. It'd barely qualify as a canal... apart from being, like, 50 miles wide from shore-to-shore. Meanwhile, Mela's Fangs are apparently fresh water (melt water?) lakes.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429133#post1429133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pneuma means lung. Or maybe rubber.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pneuma means &quot;breath&quot; or &quot;air&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-20-2020, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T05:34:18-08:00","id":1429138,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> thank you. This is really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T08:41:01-08:00","id":1429148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyper Prime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf#post1429124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where in your campaigns have you put the Bull of the Norf' and his war with house Tepet? what is the size of his dominion and how has it grown as the game progressed? How has it affected canon locations and cities?<br /> I'm asking this because as necessary as Yurgen and his funnyboys are to the set-up of exalted, his victory over the realm seem to have no impact on places like pneuma, whitewall, or the kingdom of medo in their description.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there's a tiny bit of confusion here. <br /> Exalted doesn't actually _have_ a metaplot that &quot;progresses&quot;. So it can't &quot;grow and affect&quot; things, since the books show Creation at a specific moment in history. John Doe's got it otherwise, although 8 Directions will probably discuss it more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T09:07:59-08:00","id":1429156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429148#post1429148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think there's a tiny bit of confusion here.<br /> Exalted doesn't actually _have_ a metaplot that &quot;progresses&quot;. So it can't &quot;grow and affect&quot; things, since the books show Creation at a specific moment in history. John Doe's got it otherwise, although 8 Directions will probably discuss it more.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the battle of futile blood was <i>three years </i>before the default &quot;present day&quot;/&quot;starting point of your campaign (probably)&quot;.<br /> <br /> Surely having a giant Anathema empire on your doorstep for three years would affect a location? Several locations describe how the Empress's disappearance has effected them. It's weirdly incongruous that the force that destroyed three legions and humbled the Realm hasn't made a ripple <i>anywhere </i>apart from in the Imperial City, two thousand miles away, and in whatever backwater Tepet Arada has chosen to drink himself into oblivion in.<br /> <br /> Of course, I imagine Across the 8 Directions will address it. I expect Medo (a Tepet Satrapy which is also disturbingly close to the Icewalkers) will get a nice high page count. And the Haslanti League is a fan-favorite, so I imagine they'll get a mention with a blurb on how the Bull has changed Northern politics (I believe they were trading partners in 2E).<br /> <br /> In my game, I've got him pushing even further North. Who knows what wonders he might find there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-20-2020, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T19:43:49-08:00","id":1429281,"title":"","content":"That places Bully and his horde so far out of the way as to be irrelevant, it seems like an utter waste on part of house Tepet and the realm to bother confronting Yurgen. There must be lunar warlords that are closer and a far greater threat than some random solar in the middle of nowhere. I do undestand that in the lore of the previous editions Scarlet Empress sent the Tepets off to die against Yurgen's horde before her disappearance, which is too meta, considering that the Tepet legions must have defeated other exalted warlords in the past.<br /> Also I have always disliked the fact that the kingdoms of halta and linowan got mixed up in that war, Bully's presence ruins the whole power dynamic of those two realms.<br /> Anyways I may be overthinking it, thank you all for your in-put on this matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T01:47:56-08:00","id":1429313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyper Prime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429281#post1429281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That places Bully and his horde so far out of the way as to be irrelevant, it seems like an utter waste on part of house Tepet and the realm to bother confronting Yurgen. There must be lunar warlords that are closer and a far greater threat than some random solar in the middle of nowhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I was unclear: he's literally on Malice Bay, East bank. One of the main trade arteries of the East. Literally two days away from a Tepet Satrapy (Medo).<br /> <br /> Solars only grow in threat. Especially Solars with some big manifest destiny raising a huge warlike empire two days travel away from the Realm Satrapy of Medo. Not overly far from Cherak.<br /> <br /> Looking at where Ma-Ha-Suchi, Raksi and Leviathan are based, I really doubt there was a closer Lunar Anthema.<br /> <br /> And, you gotta remember that there were only, like, a dozen Solars at the time (or, at least, there were when Yugen Exalted). Realm's most wanted.<br /> <br /> (Plus, a sorcerer can Stormwind Rider from Whitewall to Malice Bay in ten hours or so. And Hannibal marched his army on foot about a thousand miles to attack Rome -- over the alps to boot. An empire a thousand miles away might not be an immediate threat but it's still a threat.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-21-2020, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T04:47:20-08:00","id":1429331,"title":"","content":"The problem with Bull and estimating his impact on anything was always in this not having any sense in the first place.<br /> <br /> Just a cursory look at a map, comparing the place where the core of his domain is, and where the whole war that involved the Tepets took place shows the problem. namely, Bull and his horde seem to have an absolutely absurd reach, able to project power on unimaginable distances.<br /> <br /> As such, we should not even be thinking about the cities in the North. Even the inhabitants of western archipelagos should quake in their boots, afraid that Bull may show up at their doors tomorrow. Distance to him doesn't matter when he can wage war a quarter of Creation away from his home base, without seemingly having to bother with unimportant stuff like logistics, supply lines, etc.<br /> <br /> With power like that, it definitely wasn't a waste on part of house Tepet to try to squash him. Problem is, that also elevates him to the danger level that should make all the houses temporarily forget about internal tug of war in order to eliminate him asap. Because with mobility like that, he is completely capable of staging raids at the Blessed Isle itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T05:10:41-08:00","id":1429332,"title":"","content":"I don't think that holds.<br /> <br /> The war on Tepet (in 3E) specifically has the Bull falling back and contracting his nomadic forces to a position of strength, causing Tepet to over extend their supply lines.<br /> <br /> Plus, I'd be surprised if the entire Icewalker people had a population comparable to Nexus. The USA is nearly 4 million square miles, but the Native First Tribes that stretched across this vast expanse weren't a world shaking threat.<br /> <br /> Consider the size of Alexander the Great's empire. I don't think it's unreasonable.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> In 3E:<br /> <br /> The Realm, page 70 says the war occured: &quot;deeper into the icy North than anyone expected&quot;.<br /> WFHW p332 said the battle took place adjacent to the White Sea.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> (In 1E the war took place in Halta, two years <i>before</i> The Bull united the Icewalker tribes, and the Bull was a noble and rival of House Tepet. Soon after, he conquered Gethemane (four thousand miles away)... with the army he wouldn't even have for another two years. I think I can say with confidence that the Valley of Shards is no longer in Halta/the Hundred Kingdoms and the 1E fluff is a hot mess. 2E kinda fixed some of it (like removing the conquest of Gethemane and having the Bull unite the Icewalkers before the war with Tepet) but it's still a cluster-boop. The 3E fluff is very sparse, but what's written actually makes sense -- don't tar it with baggage from past editions, just take it on face value.)<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Yeah, the 1st Edition Fluff says this happened (note the Icewalkers are now on the other side of the &quot;river&quot; and closer to the White Sea in 3E)...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/vm4zSJP\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/vm4zSJP/20201221-163024.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Then Yugen marched back across the map and conquered Gethemane:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/MkHzWsr\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/MkHzWsr/20201221-163900.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Don't expect this to hold AT ALL in 3E.<br /> <br /> In 3E, the battle takes place far in the North by the White Sea and the Bull is based near Malice Bay. <i>That</i> makes sense. If Across the 8 Directions has the main battle happening thousands of miles away in Halta, then feel free to complain. But there's no indication in the published text thus far to suggest that is how it went down this time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-21-2020, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T06:26:43-08:00","id":1429350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429331#post1429331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Bull and estimating his impact on anything was always in this not having any sense in the first place.<br /> <br /> Just a cursory look at a map, comparing the place where the core of his domain is, and where the whole war that involved the Tepets took place shows the problem. namely, Bull and his horde seem to have an absolutely absurd reach, able to project power on unimaginable distances.<br /> <br /> As such, we should not even be thinking about the cities in the North. Even the inhabitants of western archipelagos should quake in their boots, afraid that Bull may show up at their doors tomorrow. Distance to him doesn't matter when he can wage war a quarter of Creation away from his home base, without seemingly having to bother with unimportant stuff like logistics, supply lines, etc.<br /> <br /> With power like that, it definitely wasn't a waste on part of house Tepet to try to squash him. Problem is, that also elevates him to the danger level that should make all the houses temporarily forget about internal tug of war in order to eliminate him asap. Because with mobility like that, he is completely capable of staging raids at the Blessed Isle itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get this logic. Just because someone can project power from point A to a far-away point B, doesn't mean they can project to a further point C.<br /> <br /> Like, what empires on Earth had a really impressive ability to project force at great distance from their home base? The Mongol Empire, for one. But the Mongol Empire wasn't a threat in France or the islands of the Pacific Ocean or anything like that, because those regions were past various obstacles blocking their ability to project power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T10:59:59-08:00","id":1429390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429332#post1429332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that holds.<br /> <br /> The war on Tepet specifically has the Bull falling back and contracting his nomadic forces to a position of strength, causing Tepet to over extend their supply lines.<br /> <br /> Plus, I'd be surprised if the entire Icewalker people had a population comparable to Nexus. The USA is nearly 4 million square miles, but the Native First Tribes that stretched across this vast expanse weren't a world shaking threat.<br /> <br /> Consider the size of Alexander the Great's empire. I don't think it's unreasonable.<br /> <br /> The Realm, page 70 says the war occured: &amp;quot;deeper into the icy North than anyone expected&amp;quot;.<br /> WFHW p332 said the battle took place adjacent to the White Sea.<br /> <br /> (In 1E the war took place in Halta, two years <i>before</i> The Bull united the Icewalker tribes, and the Bull was a noble and rival of House Tepet. Soon after, he conquered Gethemane (four thousand miles away)... with the army he wouldn't even have for another two years. I think I can say with confidence that the Valley of Shards is no longer in Halta/the Hundred Kingdoms and the 1E fluff is a hot mess.)<br /> <br /> Edit<br /> <br /> Yeah, the 1st Edition Fluff says this happened...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/vm4zSJP&amp;quot;]</a><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/vm4zSJP/20201221-163024.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>[/URL]<br /> <br /> Then Yugen marched back across the map and conquering Gethemane: <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/MkHzWsr&amp;quot;]</a><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/MkHzWsr/20201221-163900.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>[/URL]<br /> <br /> Don't expect this to hold AT ALL in 3E.<br /> <br /> In 3E, the battle takes place far in the North by the White Sea and the Bull is based near Malice Bay. That makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Once again, I agree with your analysis of Yurgen Kaneko/the Bull of the North\u2019s strategy. (Btw doesn\u2019t Kaneko mean kitten in Japanese?) Anyway, I think comparing him to Alexander the Great is a good comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T14:49:04-08:00","id":1429420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyper Prime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429281#post1429281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That places Bully and his horde so far out of the way as to be irrelevant, it seems like an utter waste on part of house Tepet and the realm to bother confronting Yurgen. There must be lunar warlords that are closer and a far greater threat than some random solar in the middle of nowhere. I do undestand that in the lore of the previous editions Scarlet Empress sent the Tepets off to die against Yurgen's horde before her disappearance, which is too meta, considering that the Tepet legions must have defeated other exalted warlords in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though you're adding assumptions here that lead to a conclusion that you dislike.<br /> <br /> If the only place that &quot;there must be more viable target and Tepet must be a House that one would expect to have won handily&quot; leads you is not satisfactory, what's the point of it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T15:36:42-08:00","id":1429425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429390#post1429390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Btw doesn\u2019t Kaneko mean kitten in Japanese?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Minton said it meant Golden Child. (But &quot;neko&quot; is cat so... lemme duck this real quick... &quot;koneko&quot; is kitten, it's close.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T15:44:27-08:00","id":1429427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429425#post1429425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Minton said it meant Golden Child. (But &amp;quot;neko&amp;quot; is cat so... lemme duck this real quick... &amp;quot;koneko&amp;quot; is kitten, it's close.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I knew I was close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T15:46:09-08:00","id":1429428,"title":"","content":"I'm setting up the Bull of the North as the next BBEG in my campaign. Totally going to use the &quot;kitten&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyper Prime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf#post1429124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where in your campaigns have you put the Bull of the Norf' and his war with house Tepet? what is the size of his dominion and how has it grown as the game progressed? How has it affected canon locations and cities?<br /> I'm asking this because as necessary as Yurgen and his funnyboys are to the set-up of exalted, his victory over the realm seem to have no impact on places like pneuma, whitewall, or the kingdom of medo in their description.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize I have posted a bunch on this topic but not actually addressed the OP, like, at all.<br /> <br /> So my campaign (Dragon-Blooded Dynast game set in the East) has covered just over a year of &quot;in game time&quot;. During this time, we've mentioned the Bull of the North as an offscreen thing. The big factor has been the fact that my character's kid wants to marry a Tepet, but my character is against it because Tepet is a fallen house and I don't want to be shackled to failure.<br /> <br /> I've kept the Bull up by Malice Bay and on the far side of Mela's Fangs, but his domain hasn't grown significantly.<br /> <br /> In my campaign, after the Battle of Futile Blood, the Bull's circle splits up and most of his empire falls apart. The Icewalker tribes push north, most of the subtergated states owe the Bull fealty in name alone -- his horde isn't powerful enough to compell tribute anymore.<br /> <br /> Raneth and Fear Eater are dead.<br /> <br /> Samea travels East, searching for a cure for Kitten and a new arm for herself. There she has made several demonic pacts and has infested the Redwood forests of Halta with demonic pine trees (<i>that</i> can only end well).<br /> <br /> Nalla Bloodaxe sits on the throne of Karn. There he seeks to build a center of civilisation as the cornerstone of the Bull's empire to rival Plenilune.<br /> <br /> Crimson Antler and the Bull himself are conducting a campaign against the Haslanti League. The Bull, in his weakened state, is unable to fight, leaving the heavy lifting to Crimson Antler. His forces were all but destroyed by the Tepets, and he lacks the demonic might Samae's bound servants granted him, whilst the Haslanti, are organized and militant. They have been able to stall his advances with their superior numbers and defensive advantages. But Crimson Antler keeps the Haslanti on the back-foot. Outlying settlements fall before the Bull, and his forces always melt away before the Haslanti can catch them (no mean feat given Haslanti airship technology).<br /> <br /> The Bull's health is fading fast, and it's likely he'll die before the year is out... but he could well die having overseen the Icewalker conquest of the Haslanti, leaving his followers with an army of airships and crossbows. Or perhaps Samea's demonic allies will provide a cure. Or perhaps... okay, I admit it... I don't actually have any idea what we're going to do after I finish the current story. But I got a few weeks to think of something. I always think of something. I mean, there's always the Eye of Autochthon if nothing else (which can segway nicely into a Locust Campaign).<br /> <br /> So whilst the Haslanti League fights against a force of Solar/Tiger Warrior guerillas, the &quot;southern&quot; cities of the North's coast remain blessedly unmolested by the Bull. They have (mostly) stopped paying tribute to the Realm (what with there being a massive Civil War on the Blessed Isle) and generally are focused on their own internal struggles. Medo breathes a little easier with the Bull thoroughly distracted (and their own Anathema, the Devil Hoofed Witch, was put down by one of my PCs) -- without an immediate security concern, they've pledged their cavalry to Mnemon's cause in the Civil War. No other location has been meaningfully impacted by the Bull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-01-2021, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T16:05:04-08:00","id":1429430,"title":"","content":"Definitely!<br /> <br /> Kitten with a Whip lol (read a book one time where that was like the title of a cheesy porn movie back in the Sixties)<br /> <br /> Bull with a Whip...hmmm. Maybe \ud83d\ude02.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T16:05:47-08:00","id":1429431,"title":"","content":"Seriously, are your PCs gonna be Dynasts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T16:16:44-08:00","id":1429432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429431#post1429431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, are your PCs gonna be Dynasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna be? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341506-dynasty-of-dovak-campaign-notes-and-play-report\">We've been playing over a year.</a> Well... we've had two new players join, retired a character, swapped a character, and retired an ST in that time... and I guess it's &quot;two Dynasts and an Outcaste who married into the Dynasty&quot;... but it's really a lot quicker just to say &quot;Dynasts&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-21-2020, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T17:50:38-08:00","id":1429445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429432#post1429432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gonna be? <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1341506-dynasty-of-dovak-campaign-notes-and-play-report&amp;quot;]We've</a> been playing over a year.[/URL] Well... we've had two new players join, retired a character, swapped a character, and retired an ST in that time... and I guess it's &amp;quot;two Dynasts and an Outcaste who married into the Dynasty&amp;quot;... but it's really a lot quicker just to say &amp;quot;Dynasts&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all Dragon-Blooded. That works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T18:39:01-08:00","id":1429450,"title":"","content":"If the Bull seems far from anywhere of immediate Realm interest it\u2019s precisely because he <i>was</i> closer until his throwdown with House Tepet ended in mutual destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T01:50:10-08:00","id":1429477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429450#post1429450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Bull seems far from anywhere of immediate Realm interest it\u2019s precisely because he <i>was</i> closer until his throwdown with House Tepet ended in mutual destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it was like a Pyrrhic victory for the Bull?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T03:20:37-08:00","id":1429482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429332#post1429332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3E, the battle takes place far in the North by the White Sea and the Bull is based near Malice Bay. <i>That</i> makes sense. If Across the 8 Directions has the main battle happening thousands of miles away in Halta, then feel free to complain. But there's no indication in the published text thus far to suggest that is how it went down this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, haven't noticed the place of battle has changed. If so, i'm withdrawing all my previous complains. Both previous editions made all his story a massive headache, something impossible to be treated seriously. If that's no longer the case, then all is good with the world again.<br /> <br /> Now even if he's limited to the north (as he should be), he is still enough of a danger for Realm to treat him seriously and send Tepets against him. Being a Solar alone is enough, but in case it wouldn't be, a reminder of Jochim should have done the trick. And definitely after the fall of the Tepet Legions, all nearby cities/satrapies should be really worrying and preparing for when (when, not if) he'll come knocking. And in case of Realm satrapies like Cherak, that includes not only local population, but also all Houses with vested interests in those lands.<br /> <br /> Now, if Bull's actions are not as all over the map as in previous editions, those Houses might not yet feel the need to cooperate (and might even think to use him against their rivals in the area), but they <i>should</i> treat him seriously.<br /> <br /> It should be even more serious matter for any local population. Houses might be afraid of their investments, but local population should be afraid for themselves. The mere fact of him defeating Realm legions (regardless of what exactly happened, and even if it was a Pyrhic victory - i doubt many people will know the details of what happened anyway) should put scare in anyone that is too close to him. Realm has some reputation as far as military might is concerned, so it would be impossible to just ignore someone that managed to pull something like that off.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T03:22:45-08:00","id":1429483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429482#post1429482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, haven't noticed the place of battle has changed. If so, i'm withdrawing all my previous complains. Both previous editions made all his story a massive headache, something impossible to be treated seriously. If that's no longer the case, then all is good with the world again.<br /> <br /> Now even if he's limited to the north (as he should be), he is still enough of a danger for Realm to treat him seriously and send Tepets against him. Being a Solar alone is enough, but in case it wouldn't be, a reminder of Jochim should have done the trick. And definitely after the fall of the Tepet Legions, all nearby cities/satrapies should be really worrying and preparing for when (when, not if) he'll come knocking. And in case of Realm satrapies like Cherak, that includes not only local population, but also all Houses with vested interests in those lands.<br /> <br /> Now, if Bull's actions are not as all over the map as in previous editions, those Houses might not yet feel the need to cooperate (and might even think to use him against their rivals in the area), but they <i>should</i> treat him seriously.<br /> <br /> It should be even more serious matter for any local population. Houses might be afraid of their investments, but local population should be afraid for themselves. The mere fact of him defeating Realm legions (regardless of what exactly happened, and even if it was a Pyrhic victory - i doubt many people will know the details of what happened anyway) should put scare in anyone that is too close to him. Realm has some reputation as far as military might is concerned, so it would be impossible to just ignore someone that managed to pull something like that off.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T08:47:14-08:00","id":1429517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429477#post1429477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it was like a Pyrrhic victory for the Bull?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It probably depends on who you ask. The Realm considers it a victory for them, and they have at least as good a claim on that: the Bull's armies were defeated and forced to retreat in the battle, and the Bull lost two of his Solar circlemates, had another lose an arm, and was badly wounded himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T09:54:50-08:00","id":1429522,"title":"","content":"Wow! So both sides took a lot of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T13:20:50-08:00","id":1429556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1429124-kingdom-of-the-bull-of-the-norf?p=1429428#post1429428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I realize I have posted a bunch on this topic but not actually addressed the OP, like, at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you JohnDoe, that helps a lot, I always felt it was a phyrric victory of some sort for the Bull of the North.<br /> I myself have consideret campaigns involving ol' Yurgen either as an ally or an enemy on many an occasion, but I always dropped them. I guess he is too big.<br /> Good luck on your campaign in the future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1131,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","user":"Hyper Prime","date":". 12-22-2020, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}